   "parent_id": null,
   "body": "Talents are wrong",
   "upvotes": 0,
   "created_at": "2026-07-30T10:40:07.735983+00:00",
   "updated_at": "2026-07-30T10:40:07.735983+00:00",
   "downvotes": 0,
   "hidden": false,
   "author": {
    "id": "8710064a-a544-4c2c-a2d4-ee6a348c7be2",
    "username": "rake2",
    "avatar_url": null
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "7ed28e29-30ec-4ff9-9fce-af4c03480dff",
   "build_id": "e9668f22-03ba-411f-a932-cb7f30d508b4",
   "author_id": "5722478d-9348-4b8a-a21e-c79a6f9163bc",
   "parent_id": null,
   "body": "Since you can only take 1 point from cap stone:\n- Barbed Quills\nNow you have an additional point left, where do you spend it:\n- Polearm Craft\nNot sure, if Bounty Hunter is worth it, but there're no additional useful slots.\n\nHere's some Q/A for rogue fans:\n\nWhy Polearm?:\nA) Question:\nTip of the Spear is the reason why it's good for AoE encounters?\nYes it has 15% chance to trigger 3 additional attacks, which does more dps if it procs.\nB) Question:\nIsn't Wild Strike uses both of your weapons like Mutilate, so two slow weapons could be more dmg in aoe encounters?\nYes it does and without Tip of the Spear talent, it's actually better to have them early.\n\nSo I need a Ranged Weapon, while I'm a melee rogue archytype?\nQuestion #1:\nSo it's no longer a stat stick?\nNo, since Quills use ranged weapon dmg it scales with your ranged weapon slot, M+ only.\nQuestion #2:\nDo I need a good ranged weapon dmg for raiding scene?\nNo, it's a stat stick there, we don't really fully utilize Quills, on certain cleave fights it's better to have one, so you are justified to take ranged weapons from actual ranged classes.\n\nAoE Mythic plus build is:\nPolearm in MH- Tip of the spear- Wildman -Quills - Polearm Craft - Barbed Quills\nSingle Target Raiding scene build is:\nSlow Dagger in MH and Fast Dagger in OH - Focused Fighter - Pilfering - Marked for Death - Barbed Quils\n\nNot sure yet, but you might be able to do this:\nSlow High Dmg in MH (Sword or Axe) - Fast Dagger in OH, before you hit 35% HP, then Swap to two daggers with (Shadowmeld+stealth or Vanish aka Woodland Adept)\nSlow High Dmg Dagger in MH - Fast Dagger remains in OH, so you can fully utilize snap shoting with our flank (ambush) thanks to Marked for Death.",
   "upvotes": 0,
